---
description: Hono on Bun — route modules, shared Zod, db package only
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# API (`apps/api`)

Bun-native server. Do not add Node, `@hono/node-server`, Express, or CORS.

```ts
// ✅ src/index.ts
app.route("/", healthRoutes);
app.route("/", workspaceRoutes);
app.route("/", projectRoutes);
```

- One Hono app per route file (`new Hono()`), then `app.route("/", …)`.
- Validate responses (and later inputs) with `@agentic-kanban/schemas`.
- Database access only through `@agentic-kanban/db` (workspace/project/board
  helpers). Never import `@libsql/client` or `drizzle-orm` from the API.
- Better Auth is wired in `src/auth/index.ts` (`betterAuth` + `drizzleAdapter`
  with `provider: "sqlite"`). `src/routes/auth.ts` mounts `/api/auth/*` via
  `auth.handler`. Do not wrap `/api/auth/*` with `@hono/zod-validator`: Better
  Auth validates the server. Client-side Zod schemas live in
  `@agentic-kanban/schemas`.
- Authz order: `auth.api.getSession({ headers: c.req.raw.headers })` → `401`
  if missing; membership via db helpers → `404` if not a member or missing
  (never `403`). Do not take `workspaceId` from query/body as permission;
  on a project, `workspace_id` comes from the row.
- `GET /api/workspaces` and `GET /api/projects/:projectId` use
  `@hono/zod-validator` (query/param) and `.parse()` the response schema.
  Board: `GET /api/projects/:projectId/board`, task create/update/delete,
  `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/move`. Comments: `GET` / `POST
  /api/tasks/:taskId/comments` (`src/routes/comments.ts`).
  POST resolves `@mentions`, writes `src/mail/outbox.ts`, then
  `publish`es `comment.created` on the project hub (after persist +
  outbox; 404 does not publish).
  Notifications: `GET /api/notifications` and
  `POST /api/notifications/:notificationId/read`
  (`src/routes/notifications.ts`; session → 401; only the session
  user's `recipient_user_id` + membership on the row's `workspace_id`;
  404 if missing/not the recipient; never 403). No
  workspace/project HTTP writes.
- Seed is `src/seed.ts` via `bun run db:seed`. Do not import it from the
  server. Users: `auth.api.signUpEmail` (reuse `user.id` if the email exists).
  Tenant rows: upsert by id / unique `(workspace_id, user_id)`. Never mass
  DELETE. Never HTTP to `/api/auth`.
- `src/middleware/rate-limit.ts` is an in-memory rate limiter for POST
  sign-up / sign-in only (not get-session). `src/middleware/session.ts`
  requires a session.
- `GET /api/projects/:projectId/events` (`src/routes/events.ts`) is
  authenticated SSE via Hono `streamSSE`. Authz matches board GET:
  `requireSession` → 401; `getProjectForMember` → 404 (never 403).
  `workspace_id` comes from the project row. On client abort, unsubscribe.
  Frames are data-only: JSON of `boardEventSchema` in `data` (no `event:`).
- `src/realtime/index.ts` is the in-process hub: `Map` of `projectId` →
  subscribers, `subscribe` / `publish`. Parse outgoing events with
  `boardEventSchema`. `publish` is a no-op with zero subscribers. Board
  writes and comment creates call `publish` after a successful row
  (`actorUserId` from the session). A 404 or validation failure does
  not publish. No Socket.IO,
  Redis, WebSocket upgrade (`ws: true`), or extra service.
- Do not auto-run migrations. Dev: `bun run --hot`. Listen
  `0.0.0.0:${API_PORT:-3000}`. Never run this API on the Mac while Compose
  is using the same `.db`.
